@@ -29,6 +30,10 @@ The planner writes `investigation.json` with this shape:
 
 Allowed severity values: `cosmetic`, `logic`, `financial`, `security`, `state-machine`. List every money, authorization, state, migration or job risk in `risks`; an empty list is an explicit claim that none applies. The runner chooses LIGHT only for bounded low-risk changes, otherwise FULL. Never downgrade risk to avoid work.
 
+`risk_areas` is required: the distinct areas the planned change itself touches, from exactly `money`, `authorization`, `state-transition`, `migration`, `background-job`. Tag an area when the implementation moves or records money, balances, ledger, escrow, fees or commissions (`money`); adds, removes or changes an auth or permission check, a role guard or who may act (`authorization`); adds, removes or changes an entity state, a transition or the guard on one (`state-transition`); adds a migration (`migration`); or changes what a worker, sweep, scheduler or other background job does or when it runs (`background-job`). Editing code that sits inside such a path without changing its behaviour, or a risk only to tests, copy, docs, deploy order or old rows, is a `risks` entry, not an area. An empty list is an explicit claim that the change touches none of them; when in doubt, tag the area. `risks` keeps every caveat worth reading, in prose.
+
+The runner also derives a ship size and a time budget from `severity`, `risks`, `risk_areas`, the submodules in `watch`, `estimated_lines`, `estimated_files` and the number of acceptance criteria, and writes them to PLAN.md as `Size:`, `Budget:`, `CI allowance:` and `Risk areas:` with the table date. S: cosmetic or logic, no `risks`, no `risk_areas`, one submodule, up to 150 lines, 5 files, 4 criteria, 90 minutes. M: cosmetic or logic, up to 500 lines, 12 files, 8 criteria, 180 minutes, either with no `risks` in one submodule or, across both submodules and whatever `risks` lists, with `risk_areas` explicitly empty (owner decision 2026-10-16); a plan without `risk_areas` gets no M by that second route. L: any tagged risk area, financial, security or state-machine severity, or anything else not S or M, up to 3000 lines, 50 files, 12 criteria, 300 minutes (owner decision 2026-10-15: raised from 1500 lines and 25 files because seven of nine prepared Sprint Ready cards estimated above the first limit). The CI wait has a separate 45-minute allowance. A missing estimate is L, never S or M. Over any L limit is XL: the runner publishes no plan, blocks the card with the exceeded limit and writes `split-proposal.md` in the card's preparation directory; the owner splits the card with `/newticket` and each part is prepared on its own. When the estimate is over an L limit, add `segments` to the investigation: a list of `{"name", "criteria": [checkItem ids], "files", "estimated_lines", "estimated_files", "depends_on": [segment names]}`, each an S, M or L on its own, so the split proposal is concrete.
+
 Map every AC exactly once, with as many independent cases as its mandatory QA coverage requires. Include failure, retry, concurrent and financial cases where relevant. Production-only observations remain separately authorized release work. Local full-suite execution is not part of preparation or shipping; keep targeted local checks and the full CI suite.
 
 `watch` names existing files or directories in `root`, `frontend` and `backend`. Include callers, consumers, shared types/configuration and intended design documents that could invalidate the plan. Watch an existing parent directory for new files. The runner conservatively expands any missing watch to its closest tracked parent and records the requested path. A read-only frontend dependency alone does not constitute frontend implementation work. The runner hashes Git objects, so unrelated commits do not invalidate a plan. Conservative directory coverage is preferable to missing a relevant dependency. The root DESIGN.md is included automatically.
